    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **25 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field on the owner API. The change spans the layers where this codebase derives computed owner attributes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema (this drives generation of `OwnerDto` at build time), alongside the existing derived fields like `membershipNumber` and `householdId`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `membershipTier` backed by a `membershipTier(Owner)` method:\n   - Returns `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount == 0` **and** an email is present (non-null, non-blank).\n   - Returns `\"BRONZE\"` otherwise.\n\nThis follows the existing pattern in the mapper (`membershipNumber`, `householdId`), so it fits the established Spring/MapStruct idiom. I confirmed that unique owners get `namesakeCount = 0` (not null) on creation via `ClinicServiceImpl.countNamesakes`, so the SILVER case triggers correctly for the test scenario, while the default owner payload (no email) yields BRONZE.",
